cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Resistance determinants in industrial effluent metagenomes
message: If you use this software or these results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jadeja
    given-names: Niti B.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2199-9605"
    affiliation: University of Virginia School of Medicine
repository-code: "https://github.com/jadejaniti/amr-metagenome-screen"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible screen of two publicly deposited metagenome assemblies from
  pharmaceutical and industrial effluent treatment in India for antimicrobial
  resistance genes, biocide resistance determinants, class 1 integron markers
  and plasmid replicons. Includes the alignment and locus-resolution scripts,
  the full and non-redundant result sets for both assemblies, and a statement
  of the limits that assembly fragmentation places on linkage claims.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - metagenomics
  - class 1 integrons
  - mobile genetic elements
  - industrial effluent
  - resistome
license: MIT
